polynomial with respect to n.

The terms of the bet are *not* that a quantum computer can
solve all NP complete problems, and *not* that a
quantum computer can improve the running time of
parallelizable algorithms.

Evidence that a quantum computer is irrelevant to speeding
up parallelizable algorithms is also irrelevant to this
bet.  Nobody is claiming that quantum parallelism is
relevant to algorithmic parallelism, and there is good
reason to believe that it is irrelevant.

A quantum computer cannot run classical algorithms more
efficiently than a classical computer.  It can however
perform algorithms that have no classical equivalent.

